IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa7-ch2`
IMPORT `coa7-ch3a`
IMPORT `coa7-ch5`

-- coa7-regulative.l4: five of the Part 13 duties that carry a time limit in days, written as regulative rules
-- (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... HENCE ... LEST ...) over the core's generic `Action of a party`, whose first
-- actor field is the performer. Layer 1, tested by #TRACE and, beside each trace, by an #ASSERT on the decision
-- function of the same duty (its "twin" in coa7-ch2, coa7-ch3a and coa7-ch5), which is the check this binary can
-- count: a #TRACE prints FULFILLED or a breach or a residual obligation, never an assertion line.
--
-- WITHIN counts from the moment the obligation is entered (the day numbers in the traces are days after that
-- moment), so the rule's "21 days" runs from the time the duty arises, as the text of each section says. A duty
-- whose time limit counts from a date the person states (not from the arming of the rule) is the twin's job.
-- On the stable binary the performer named after PARTY must be the first actor of the action; `main` does not check
-- a mismatch, so each rule below is read by eye (dialects.md, "Silent").

§ `Part 13 -- duties with a time limit, as regulative rules`

-- src:3847 | (3) The company must send or submit the copies (or, if copies are sent or submitted to members on different days, the first of those copies) not more than 21 days after it becomes subject to the requirement under section 292 to circulate the resolution.
@ref s 293(3) Circulation of written resolution proposed by members: within 21 days (regulative rule) (src:3847)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 293(3) the company must send or submit the copies within 21 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send or submit the copies of the resolution to every eligible member"
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not send or submit the copies within 21 days after becoming subject to the requirement under section 292 (s 293(3))"

-- src:3914 | (1) Directors required under section 303 to call a general meeting of the company must call a meeting—
-- src:3915 | (a) within 21 days from the date on which they become subject to the requirement, and
@ref s 304(1)(a) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: within 21 days (regulative rule) (src:3914-3915)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 304(1)(a) the directors must call the meeting within 21 days` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Member, "call the general meeting"
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors did not call the meeting within 21 days from the date on which they became subject to the requirement (s 304(1)(a))"

-- src:4408 | (1) Directors who are required under section 342 to obtain an independent report on a poll or polls must appoint a person they consider to be appropriate (an “independent assessor”) to prepare a report for the company on it or them.
-- src:4409 | (2) The appointment must be made within one week after the company being required to obtain the report.
@ref s 343(2) Appointment of independent assessor: within one week (regulative rule) (src:4408-4409)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 343(2) the directors must appoint the independent assessor within one week` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "appoint an independent assessor to prepare a report"
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors did not appoint an independent assessor within one week after the company was required to obtain the report (s 343(2))"

-- src:4384 | (1B) A traded company must comply with subsection (1A) by—
-- src:4385 | (a) the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting, or
-- src:4386 | (b) if later, the end of the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared.
@ref s 341(1B) Results of poll to be made available on website: within 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting (regulative rule) (src:4384-4386)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 341(1B) the traded company must make the poll results available within 16 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "make the poll results available on a website"
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the traded company did not make the poll results available on a website by the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting (s 341(1B)(a))"

-- src:4647 | (3) The information under subsection (1) must be provided to the member as soon as reasonably practicable and in any event by the end of the period of 15 days beginning with whichever is the later of the first working day after the day on which—
-- src:4648 | (a) the result of the poll is declared for that resolution; or
-- src:4649 | (b) the request for information under subsection (2)(a) is received by the company.
@ref s 360BA(3) Traded companies: right to confirmation of vote: within 15 days (regulative rule) (src:4647-4649)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 360BA(3) the traded company must provide the information within 15 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "provide information enabling the member to confirm that the vote was validly recorded and counted"
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the traded company did not provide the information by the end of the period of 15 days beginning with the later first working day (s 360BA(3))"

-- ---- s 304(1)(a): 21 days. The rule is entered at day 0 (the day the directors become subject to the requirement).
-- on time (day 21) and late (day 22), against the twin `s 304(1)(a) the directors called the meeting in time`
#TRACE `s 304(1)(a) the directors must call the meeting within 21 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `Action of a party` OF Director, Member, "call the general meeting" AT 21
#TRACE `s 304(1)(a) the directors must call the meeting within 21 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `Action of a party` OF Director, Member, "call the general meeting" AT 22
-- nobody else's act discharges the duty (the company calls the meeting; the duty is the directors')
#TRACE `s 304(1)(a) the directors must call the meeting within 21 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "call the general meeting" AT 10
#ASSERT `s 304(1)(a) the directors called the meeting in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 22 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304(1)(a) the directors called the meeting in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 293(3): 21 days
#TRACE `s 293(3) the company must send or submit the copies within 21 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send or submit the copies of the resolution to every eligible member" AT 21
#TRACE `s 293(3) the company must send or submit the copies within 21 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send or submit the copies of the resolution to every eligible member" AT 22
#ASSERT `s 293(3) the copies were sent or submitted in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 22 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 293(3) the copies were sent or submitted in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 23 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 343(2): one week
#TRACE `s 343(2) the directors must appoint the independent assessor within one week` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "appoint an independent assessor to prepare a report" AT 7
#TRACE `s 343(2) the directors must appoint the independent assessor within one week` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `Action of a party` OF Director, Company, "appoint an independent assessor to prepare a report" AT 8
#ASSERT `s 343(2) the appointment was made in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 343(2) the appointment was made in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 341(1B): 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting (day 0 is the day of the meeting, so the last day is day 15)
#TRACE `s 341(1B) the traded company must make the poll results available within 16 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "make the poll results available on a website" AT 15
#TRACE `s 341(1B) the traded company must make the poll results available within 16 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "make the poll results available on a website" AT 16
#ASSERT `s 341(1B) the traded company has complied with subsection (1A) in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 341(1B) the traded company has complied with subsection (1A) in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 360BA(3): 15 days beginning with the later first working day (day 0): the last day is day 14
#TRACE `s 360BA(3) the traded company must provide the information within 15 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "provide information enabling the member to confirm that the vote was validly recorded and counted" AT 14
#TRACE `s 360BA(3) the traded company must provide the information within 15 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "provide information enabling the member to confirm that the vote was validly recorded and counted" AT 15
#ASSERT `s 360BA(3) the information was provided in time` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 360BA(3) the information was provided in time` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
